    "measurementTechnique": [
      "Experimental design: Three launch sites per experiment day were deployed across three locations in Chicago. The sites were selected to contrast different urban settings: downtown Chicago (Shedd Aquarium), the West Side (Humboldt Park), and the South Side (Gary Comer Youth Center/West Woodlawn).\nField collection methods: A 39-hour period was sampled in each intensive observing period (IOP) by three independent launch teams. Soundings were coordinated across sites to begin launches nearly simultaneously in order to facilitate comparisons across sites. Kestrel meteorological instrument surface measurements were collected at the time of each launch in order to facilitate instrument calibration and detect instrument anomalies.\nData QC: Data QC used Kestrel weather sensor measurements at the ground sites to check the near-surface values of the sondes. For the DFM-19 sondes, pressure measurements from the Kestrels were used to compute the initial pressure of the sondes, since the sondes do not have a barometer. The NCAR/EOL Aspen v4.0.3 upsonde quality control procedure was applied to the sondes, which removes spurious temperature and humidity lapse rates and outlier winds. This QC procedure produces final data products in netCDF format contain 1-s values of temperature, dewpoint, pressure, geopotential height, and earth-relative u- and v-wind components. Quick look Skew-T log-p diagrams are provided from Aspen.\nKnown limitations of the data: Some sensors failed at measuring humidity after launch, and missing values are reported in the final dataset. Users are directed"
    ],
